# Every setting hi reads, one row each, in the order docs/SETTINGS.md's
# _Every setting_ table lists them: the table is written from these rows
# (.github/prettier-plugin-docs.mjs), and `hi --configure` writes settings.sh
# a line a row in the same order (scripts/configure.sh's _hi_settings_load).
#
# <section> | <name> | <default> | <check> | <hint> | <what it does>
#
# <section> is preset for a setting every preset answers, back to its
# default where the preset names none, and you for the rest (the table's
# "set by" column follows from it). <check> is the kind of value it takes,
# scripts/lib.sh's _hi_setting_check reads it, and <hint> says it in words:
# `hi --doctor` judges a value by them, - for none. <default> and <what it
# does> are the table's cells, in Markdown; a <default> of one code span is
# also the value settings.sh's commented line shows. No column holds a
# ` | `; a `|` inside one is written `\|`.

preset | _HI_DISABLE_HEADER | `0` | toggle | 1 or 0 | turns off the whole header, on connect, on disconnect, and in a local shell; a connect then sends no header code
you | _HI_HEADER_ORDER | the table in [Header details](#header-details) | header | words from | which header items show, and in what order; empty is the default list
you | _HI_MAX_WIDTH | `80` | number:40 | a number, 40 or more | the columns the header is drawn to, or fewer on a narrower terminal; 40 at least
preset | _HI_PACKAGES_GROUPS | `core deprecated` | groups | none, or group names like core useful | the `config/packages` groups the header's check runs, or `none`; `base` adds the tools hi itself uses ([the package check](COLORS.md#the-package-checks-rows))
you | _HI_IP_HIDE | `docker* br-* podman* cni-podman* virbr* lxdbr* incusbr*` | globs | none, or globs like docker* 10.0.* | globs of addresses or interface names the header's `ip` cell hides; `none` hides nothing ([Header details](#header-details))
preset | _HI_DISABLE_GIT_STATUS | `0` | toggle | 1 or 0 | turns off the prompt's git segment
preset | _HI_DISABLE_ENV_STATUS | `0` | toggle | 1 or 0 | turns off the prompt's `(myproj)` environment segment ([Integrations](INTEGRATIONS.md#the-environment-segment))
preset | _HI_TOOL_ALIASES | `0` | flag | 1 or 0 | `1` turns on the `cat`, `bat`, `ls`, and `eza` aliases ([Integrations](INTEGRATIONS.md#bat-and-eza))
preset | _HI_SUDO_ALIAS | `0` | flag | 1 or 0 | `1` turns on the `sudo` alias, so `sudo vim` keeps the vim alias's flags
preset | _HI_DISABLE_LOCAL | `0` | toggle | 1 or 0 | turns off everything above, and the banner, **on this machine only**; targets still get hi ([Others](#others))
preset | _HI_DISABLE_PROMPT | `0` | toggle | 1 or 0 | turns off hi's prompt, leaving your shell's own
you | _HI_PROMPT_TOOL | unset | prompts | hi, or a program, each optionally bash:, zsh:, or fish: for a shell it fits - the programs are | who draws the prompt: a list of `powerlevel10k`, `oh-my-zsh`, `oh-my-bash`, `bash-it`, `tide`, `starship`, `oh-my-posh`, `powerline-go`, and `hi`; unset, every one installed here ([Integrations](INTEGRATIONS.md#prompt-programs))
you | _HI_PROMPT_END_BASH | `\$` | noquote | a single quote can't be written to settings.sh | bash's prompt separator (`\$` is `$`, or `#` for root); also the prompt of a target without bash
you | _HI_PROMPT_END_ZSH | `%(!.#.>)` | noquote | a single quote can't be written to settings.sh | zsh's prompt separator; zsh prompt escapes work
you | _HI_PROMPT_END_FISH | `\|` | noquote | a single quote can't be written to settings.sh | fish's prompt separator; unset, root gets `#`
you | _HI_DISABLE_LEAD_SPACE | `0` | flag | 1 or 0 | `1` drops the leading space before the prompt and each header row
you | _HI_DISABLE_RIGHT_EDGE | `0` | flag | 1 or 0 | `1` drops the closing \| from every header row
you | _HI_PLUGINS_ON | unset | plugins | plugins that hi --plugins lists (hi --configure converts a group's word) | plugins that are off by default (`hooks`, `env`, `git`) to turn on; `hi --enable-plugin` writes it ([Switching a plugin off](#switching-a-plugin-off))
preset | _HI_PLUGINS_OFF | unset | plugins | plugins or members that hi --plugins lists (hi --configure converts a group's word) | plugins or files that stay home; `hi --disable-plugin` writes it ([Switching a plugin off](#switching-a-plugin-off))
you | _HI_KEEP | `0` | flag | 1 or 0 | `1` makes every ssh connect a `--keep` one; `--no-keep` skips it once ([Integrations](INTEGRATIONS.md#terminal-multiplexers))
you | _HI_UPDATE_UNSIGNED | `0` | flag | 1 or 0 | `1` lets `hi --update` take a tag it cannot verify (unsigned, an unknown key, or no gpg), saying which; a bad signature refuses either way ([Security](SECURITY.md#what-hi-does---and-deliberately-doesnt))
preset | _HI_PLAIN | `0` | flag | 1 or 0 | `1` makes every connect a `--plain` one, sending nothing; `--no-plain` skips it once. Most useful in a tag's file ([Settings by host tag](#settings-by-host-tag))
you | _HI_KEEP_TIMEOUT | `24h` | duration | seconds, or a number with s, m, h, or d | how long a kept session waits with nobody attached before it closes; `0` is never. Read on the target
you | _HI_HOLD_TIMEOUT | `15m` | duration | seconds, or a number with s, m, h, or d | how long a dropped session's files wait for a reconnect on a target with no multiplexer; `0` holds nothing. Read on the target
you | _HI_KEEP_RETRY | `5m` | duration | seconds, or a number with s, m, h, or d | how long hi retries a kept session after the link drops; `0` is never
you | _HI_DISABLE_KEEP | `0` | flag | 1 or 0 | `1` turns kept sessions off: `--keep` and `--end` are refused, and `tmux`, `zellij`, and `screen` are the plain tools ([Integrations](INTEGRATIONS.md#terminal-multiplexers))
you | _HI_SHELL_PREFERENCE | `login` | shells | login, bash, zsh, fish, in order | the shells a session tries, in order: `login` (your login shell on the target), `bash`, `zsh`, or `fish`; the first the target has wins. Read on the target
you | _HI_BACKENDS_OFF | unset | - | - | backends hi never asks (`docker`, `podman`, `nerdctl`, `finch`, `nomad`, `kube`), or `all` for ssh alone; `--use` still reaches one ([Compatibility](COMPATIBILITY.md#what-ships))
you | _HI_DISABLE_CONTROLMASTER | `0` | flag | 1 or 0 | `1` stops hi passing ssh its `ControlMaster` options, so your ssh config decides; a connect then authenticates twice ([Security](SECURITY.md#trust-boundaries))
you | _HI_TRUECOLOR | by terminal | flag | 1, 0, or unset for the terminal's own verdict | `1` or `0` forces or refuses 24-bit color; unset, the terminal decides ([Colors](COLORS.md))
you | _HI_EDITOR | unset | editor | one of | the editor a session sets as `$EDITOR`, `$VISUAL`, and `$SUDO_EDITOR`, where the target has it; unset, your own `$EDITOR`, else the first of `nvim vim micro hx helix kak nano emacs` the target has
you | _HI_POWERLINE_GO_OPTS | unset | - | - | extra flags for [powerline-go](https://github.com/justjanne/powerline-go) (`-modules venv,cwd,git -mode flat`)
you | NO_COLOR | unset | - | - | [the convention](https://no-color.org): any non-empty value turns off color, on targets too
you | _HI_LS_OPTS | `-F -1 -l -m --group-directories-first --smart-group` + a time format where eza answers, else `-F -l` (and `--color=auto` where `ls` takes it) | - | - | the flags of the `ls`/`eza` alias; set, it replaces hi's
you | _HI_BAT_OPTS | `-P --tabs 2 --style changes,grid` | - | - | the flags of the `bat`/`batn` aliases; no `--theme`, so your bat config's theme shows
